      "output": {
        "message": "Here are three practical ways to start shifting your evenings: 1. **Find a low-pressure spot outside the house.** Pick a local coffee shop open late, a gym, a library, or a neighborhood park, and go at the same time once or twice a week. It gets you out and around familiar faces without the pressure to initiate conversation immediately.\n2. **Join an activity with built-in structure.** Groups centered on a specific task—like a run club, a board game meetup, a pottery class, or casual rec sports—make interaction much easier because you are focusing on the activity rather than small talk.\n3. **Decide if you want company or just engagement.** If you want to meet people, browse local event pages (like Meetup, Eventbrite, or a city subreddit) for one event this week. If you simply want your evenings to feel less empty, set up a deliberate project, class, or a weekly call with an old friend so staying in feels like an intentional choice. Does getting out of the apartment appeal more right now, or are you looking to meet people directly?",
